OpenMP for periodic-lattice solves (pyMSTM 2.1).

Applied on top of mstm-modules-33-f2py-data-fix.patch, to the copy of
mstm-modules-33.f90 compiled into the Python extension only (the MSTM CLI
builds from the unmodified upstream source). Parallelises the one hot loop
of a periodic-lattice solve; with pl_num_threads = 1 (the default) the
upstream code path runs unchanged.

periodic_lattice_sphere_interaction: every solver iteration (MSTM does not
store the matrices unless store_translation_matrix, which pyMSTM keeps
off) loops over all sphere pairs (i,j), computes the lattice-summed pair
matrix with plane_boundary_lattice_interaction and applies it to the
right-hand sides. With pl_num_threads > 1 the pair matrices are computed
in parallel ahead of that loop, a chunk of consecutive pairs (in the loop's
own order, at most pl_chunk_elements matrix elements) at a time; the loop
then copies each matrix instead of computing it. Pair order, nmat
numbering, storage and the order in which the matrices are applied to aout
are the serial code's, so results are bit-identical for any thread count.
finite_lattice (a test option; uses gentranmatrix and its saved state)
stays serial.

Shared state written by plane_boundary_lattice_interaction and its callees
(audited: periodic_lattice_subroutines, layer_gf/layer_gfos/layer_gfrec,
and the specialfuncs routines they call, which only read saved constants
and the numconstants tables):
- COMMON /qkernelcommon/: the parameters of the q1d/q2d integrands, set in
  q2db/q1dbnosource and read in qkernel1d/qkernel2d -> threadprivate.
- pl_max_subdivs (reset and read back within one matrix), pl_fs_method,
  pl_rs_imax, q1d/q2d_number_segments, time_0, time_count (diagnostics),
  number_gf_iterations (reset in layer_gf, read in layer_gfos) ->
  threadprivate, and hidden from f2py (a thread-local address is
  meaningless to Python).
- pl_error_codes(:), error_codes(1): "something did not converge" flags,
  read after the solve -> stay shared, set with atomic writes.
New module variables: pl_num_threads (default 1; set from Python through
the f2py module attribute) and pl_chunk_elements (default 4194304 complex
numbers = 64 MiB of pair matrices per chunk).

